-- smucclaw/l4-ide#1076. The mixfix rule below is under a `§`, and it has the
-- word `the day`. The two rules after it have an INPUT called `the day`, and
-- pass that input on as the argument of another rule. The input is the rule's
-- own, so inside the rule it is the input and not the word of the mixfix rule.
-- It was read as the word, a postfix use of the mixfix rule applied to `inc`,
-- and refused ("You are giving 1 input to `the day` ... but it is not a
-- function"), and every importer then got #1025's internal error.
§ `Lib`
GIVEN n IS A NUMBER
      s IS A NUMBER
`the day` n `days before` s MEANS s MINUS n

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`inc` `the day` MEANS `the day` PLUS 1

GIVEN `the day` IS A NUMBER
GIVETH A NUMBER
`twice` `the day` MEANS `inc` `the day`

-- In a rule with no input of that name, the word is still the word.
#EVAL `the day` 3 `days before` 10    -- 7
#EVAL `inc` 5                         -- 6
#EVAL `twice` 5                       -- 6
